1
00:05:45,714 --> 00:05:51,714
The Five Heartbeats is a drama, music film directed by Robert Townsend.

2
00:11:31,428 --> 00:11:37,428
In the early 1960s, a quintet of hopeful, young African-American men
form an amateur vocal group called The Five Heartbeats.

3
00:17:17,142 --> 00:17:23,142
After an initially rocky start, the group improves, turns pro,
and rises to become a top flight music sensation.

4
00:23:02,857 --> 00:23:08,857
Along the way, however, the guys learn many hard lessons
about the reality of the music industry.

5
00:28:48,571 --> 00:28:54,571
Duck, played by Robert Townsend.

6
00:34:34,285 --> 00:34:40,285
Eddie, played by Michael Wright.

7
00:40:20,000 --> 00:40:26,000
J.T., played by Leon.

8
00:46:05,714 --> 00:46:11,714
Dresser, played by Harry Lennix.

9
00:51:51,428 --> 00:51:57,428
Choirboy, played by Tico Wells.

10
00:57:37,142 --> 00:57:43,142
Eleanor Potter, played by Diahann Carroll.

11
01:03:22,857 --> 01:03:28,857
The Five Heartbeats is a 1991 musical drama film directed by Robert
Townsend, who co-wrote the script with Keenen Ivory Wayans.

12
01:09:08,571 --> 01:09:14,571
Produced and distributed by 20th Century Fox, the film's main cast
includes Townsend, Michael Wright, Leon Robinson, Harry J.

13
01:14:54,285 --> 01:15:00,285
Lennix, Tico Wells, John Canada Terrell, Harold Nicholas, and Diahann Carroll.

14
01:20:40,000 --> 01:20:46,000
The plot of the film (which is loosely based on the lives of several artists: The Dells, The Temptations, Four Tops, Wilson Pickett, James
Brown, Frankie Lymon, Sam Cooke and others) follows the three decade career of the rhythm and blues vocal group The Five Heartbeats.

15
01:26:25,714 --> 01:26:31,714
The film depicts the rise and fall of a Motown-inspired soul act through
the eyes of one of the Heartbeats, Donald "Duck" Matthews.

16
01:32:11,428 --> 01:32:17,428
The film was released to most North American audiences on March 29, 1991; however, it was not made
available to audiences in other continents until 2002, when a DVD was released.

17
01:37:57,142 --> 01:38:03,142
Another DVD was released in 2006 for the film's 15th anniversary.

18
01:43:42,857 --> 01:43:48,857
Even though the movie received mixed reviews from critics at the time of its release, it became a
cult classic through VHS rentals, with many calling it Townsend's masterpiece.

19
01:49:28,571 --> 01:49:34,571
The film explores themes of rhythm and blues (r&b), battle of the bands, 1960s.

20
01:55:14,285 --> 01:55:20,285
The tone is uplifting and emotional.
